```text
MEMORANDUM

To:

Mayor Orr, City Council

From:
Nathan Beauheim, P.E., Transportation Administrator

Subject:
Sole Source Purchase of Traffic Signal Software and Hardware from AM
Signal

Date:
May 9, 2018

Attached for consideration is a sole source purchase of traffic signal software and
hardware from AM Signal, Inc. of Littleton, CO.  The primary reason for procuring the
system in this fashion is to maintain consistency with WYDOT, who purchased this
system late last year after engaging in a nearly year-long procurement process.

The procurement process for WYDOT began with initial presentations from interested
vendors based on a set of system requirements created by WYDOT.  After the initial
presentations, selected vendors were invited to demonstrate their wares during a 30-
day on-street trial on Grand Ave. in Laramie.  The selected vendors were then invited to
bid head-to-head on supplying the various system components.  AM Signal was the
successful vendor from that process to supply the MaxView/MaxTime system and
associated hardware from Intelight.  As is typical within the traffic industry, AM Signal is
the only vendor authorized to sell Intelight products within their geographic territory.

This procurement consists of the following components:

MaxView software – this software resides on the City servers and is the
component that allows the City to remotely monitor and program traffic signals
across the City.  This software also includes a number of capabilities that the City
currently lacks, such as the ability to automatically generate alerts of faults,
better logging of events, and significantly more analytics.  We are proposing to
acquire licenses for 80 intersections, which is sufficient to cover all current and
planned signals with a few left over.  The quote also establishes pricing for up to
ten years of maintenance and support.

MaxTime software – this software resides on the controller at the individual
intersections.  While a set of protocols exists (known as NTCIP) that are
supposed to allow equipment from different manufacturers to work together, in

A COMMUNITY OF CHOICE

PUBLIC WORKS DEPARTMENT
2101 O’Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001
