### Page 2 of 12

```text
Sole Source Purchase of Traffic Signal Software and Hardware from AM Signal
May 9, 2018
Page 2 of 2

practice full utilization of features requires purchase of the full suite of products
from a given manufacturer.  The software the City is currently using is no longer
being supported by the manufacturer, so this upgrade is timely from that
perspective as well.

2070LDX Controllers – this hardware resides at the individual intersections.
These twenty-two controllers are state of the art and will be used to upgrade the
most critical intersections.

2070-1C Module – this hardware will be used to upgrade older controllers to run
the new controller software.  This is necessary as the older controllers run OS9
as their operating system while the new controller software requires Linux.

NEMA X3L Controllers – this hardware resides at the individual intersections.
These will be used to upgrade the hardware at intersections with older control
equipment.  We investigated several different methods of upgrading the existing
controllers without success before deciding to purchase new equipment.

Should this contract be approved, AM Signal proposes to have all equipment delivered,
software installed, and the system running by September 30, 2018.
